---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/post.css';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy | Opera Shalem" noindex description="How Opera Shalem collects, uses, and protects personal data, and your rights under GDPR and Israeli privacy law.">
  <main>
    <article class="blog-post-page">
      <header class="post-header">
        <h1 class="post-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <div class="post-meta">
          <span class="post-date">Last updated: 2 November 2026</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="post-content">
        <p>This policy explains what personal data the Opera Shalem website (operashalem.com) collects, why, and what rights you have. It is written to meet the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and Israel's Protection of Privacy Law, 5741-1981, as amended.</p>

        <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>

        <p>Opera Shalem is a cultural initiative in formation, based in Jerusalem, Israel. It has not yet been incorporated as a legal entity. Until it is, the controller responsible for personal data collected through this website is <mark class="todo">[TO CONFIRM: name of the person responsible, on behalf of the founding team]</mark>.</p>

        <p>You can reach us about anything in this policy at <a href="mailto:info@operashalem.com">info@operashalem.com</a>. When Opera Shalem is incorporated, we will update this policy to name the new entity.</p>

        <h2>2. What we collect</h2>

        <h3>When you use the contact form or email us</h3>
        <p>We collect the details you give us: your name, email address, area of interest, your message, and anything else you choose to include. Giving us this information is voluntary and not required by law, but we cannot reply without a way to contact you.</p>

        <h3>When you visit the site</h3>
        <p>Our website is delivered by Cloudflare. To deliver pages and protect the site against abuse, Cloudflare processes technical information about each request, such as your IP address, browser type, the page requested, and the date and time. We do not keep our own visitor logs, and we do not use this information to identify or profile visitors.</p>

        <h3>Fonts</h3>
        <p>Our pages load a typeface from an external font service (fonts.cdnfonts.com). To deliver the font, that service receives your IP address and browser details. We do not control how it uses that data.</p>

        <h3>What we don't do</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>We do not set cookies or use analytics, advertising, or tracking tools. Cloudflare may set strictly necessary security cookies to protect the site from abuse.</li>
            <li>We do not sell or rent personal data, or share it with anyone for their own marketing.</li>
            <li>The social media icons are plain links. No data is sent to those platforms unless you click through, after which their own privacy policies apply.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Why we use it, and on what legal basis</h2>

        <ul>
            <li><strong>To reply to your enquiry and continue the conversation you started,</strong> including about partnership. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in responding to people who contact us, and, where you are discussing an arrangement with us, taking steps at your request before entering into an agreement (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f) and 6(1)(b)).</li>
            <li><strong>To keep the website running and secure.</strong> Legal basis: our legitimate interest in operating a secure site (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)).</li>
            <li><strong>To meet legal obligations,</strong> if any apply (GDPR Art. 6(1)(c)).</li>
        </ul>

        <p>We will not add you to any mailing list without your explicit consent.</p>

        <h2>4. Who receives your data</h2>

        <p>We share personal data only with service providers that process it on our behalf, and only as needed to provide their service:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Cloudflare, Inc. (United States): website hosting, delivery, and security, including running the contact form.</li>
            <li>Resend (Plus Five Five, Inc., United States): delivering contact form submissions to our inbox by email.</li>
            <li>IONOS SE (Germany): our email mailbox, where enquiries and correspondence are stored.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We may also disclose data if required by law, or to protect our rights or the safety of others.</p>

        <h2>5. International transfers</h2>

        <p>We are based in Israel, which the European Commission recognises as providing an adequate level of data protection. Our service providers in the United States handle data under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses.</p>

        <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>

        <p>We keep enquiries and correspondence for as long as we need them to respond and to follow up on the conversation, and no longer than <mark class="todo">[TO CONFIRM: e.g. 24 months]</mark> after our last contact with you, unless we have an ongoing relationship or a legal reason to keep them longer.</p>

        <h2>7. Your rights</h2>

        <p>Depending on where you live, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>access the personal data we hold about you and receive a copy;</li>
            <li>have inaccurate data corrected or completed;</li>
            <li>have your data deleted;</li>
            <li>restrict or object to our use of your data, including where we rely on legitimate interests;</li>
            <li>receive your data in a portable format;</li>
            <li>withdraw any consent you have given, at any time, without affecting earlier processing.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:info@operashalem.com">info@operashalem.com</a>. We will respond within one month. We may need to confirm your identity first.</p>

        <p>If you are unhappy with how we have handled your data, please contact us first. You also have the right to complain to a data protection authority: in the EU, the supervisory authority in your country of residence or work; in the UK, the Information Commissioner's Office; in Israel, the Privacy Protection Authority at the Ministry of Justice.</p>

        <h2>8. Children</h2>

        <p>This website is not directed at children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect their personal data. If you believe a child has sent us personal data, please contact us and we will delete it.</p>

        <h2>9. Security</h2>

        <p>The site and contact form are served only over encrypted connections (HTTPS), and we limit access to enquiries to the people who need to respond to them. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but we take reasonable measures to protect your data.</p>

        <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>

        <p>We will update this policy when our practices change, including when Opera Shalem is incorporated. The date at the top of the page shows when it was last revised.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>

